From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:24:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 21/30] gunyah + aarch64: iceland gvm:
 --protected-vm-pseudo-unprotected, the opt-in shared memory mode (after
 DroidVM)

Ported from DroidVM dvm-crosvm 849e05f (GPL-2.0-or-later + ADDITIONAL-PERMISSIONS, headers kept; CREDITS lists it),
re-plumbed onto our host kernel's patch 0008 instead of DroidVM's out-of-tree share module:
- ProtectionType::ProtectedPseudoUnprotected (isolates_memory, shares_guest_ram), cmdline flag, Gunyah only, no
  default swiotlb.
- Layout: a 4 MiB lent boot region (the compiled-in boot shim at its base, the device tree at +2 MiB), a 2 MiB shared
  handoff page (MemoryRegionPurpose::ShimHandoff, shm vdevice), the rest of --mem as the window
  (MemoryRegionPurpose::SharedGuestRam: not registered at VM creation, not in /memory, no shm vdevice). The payload
  goes to the window's base; the hypervisor starts the shim.
- After GH_VM_START the window is shared with GH_VM_PROTECTED_SHARE (guest R/W/X; ICELAND_SHIM_PARCEL_MB splits it),
  the handles go into the handoff page and `ready` is set last; a watcher thread turns the shim's status into
  GH-SHIM log lines. ICELAND_SHIM_PROBE_EXEC / ICELAND_SHIM_NO_EXEC are diagnostics.
The host can read and write all of such a VM's RAM: the app offers it only as an explicit per-VM opt-in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
